syntax error.example:
$total = 5
echo $total;   // PHP complains here; the semicolon is missing above
$total = 5;

Undefined variable.example:
$total = 5;
echo $totl;                   // spelled differently
echo $total;
echo $maybe ?? 'default';     // ?? supplies a value when it is unset

Undefined array key.example:
$ages = ['sam' => 12];
echo $ages['Sam'];              // capital S is a different key
echo $ages['Sam'] ?? 0;         // ?? gives a default instead

Call to undefined function.example:
echo strlen('abc');    // a real built-in
echo strLen('abc');    // PHP function names are case-insensitive,
                       // but your OWN functions must match how they were defined

TypeError.example:
function double(int $n) { return $n * 2; }
double('abc');       // not a number
double((int) '12');  // convert first

ArgumentCountError.example:
function greet($name, $greeting) { }
greet('Ada');                              // one argument short
function greetOk($name, $greeting = 'Hi') { }   // a default makes it optional

Error.example:
$user = null;
$user->getName();     // null is not an object
if ($user !== null) { $user->getName(); }

Exception.example:
try {
    risky();
} catch (Exception $e) {
    echo 'Could not do it: ' . $e->getMessage();
}

Undefined property.example:
class User { public $name; }
$u = new User();
echo $u->nmae;    // spelled differently
echo $u->name;

Undefined method.example:
class User { function getName() { } }
$u = new User();
$u->getname();    // your own method names ARE case-insensitive in PHP,
$u->getName();    // but matching how you defined it keeps the code readable
